  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/he-c/6912",
  "definition": "Access to Child Care Settings",
  "effectiveDate": "2020-07-01",
  "historyNote": "#13064, eff 7-1-20",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "He-C 6912.14",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-c6900.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-C 6912.14 Access to Child Care Settings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-C 6912.14 Access to Child Care Settings.\n\n(a) An enrolled child care provider shall allow a parent access to his or her child(ren) at all times while the child(ren) is in the child care provider’s care, unless allowing access is contrary to a court order or a court-ordered parenting plan.\n\n(b) An enrolled child care provider shall upon request, share information about a child’s needs and progress with the parent or authorized DHHS staff, unless sharing information with the parent is contrary to a court order.\n\n(c) An enrolled child care provider shall allow authorized DHHS staff to visit, during the time a child receives child care, to observe the child to ensure the health or safety of the child in the child care setting.\n\n(d) An enrolled child care provider shall allow authorized DHHS staff to visit during operating hours when DCYF has received a complaint about a child’s health or safety in the child care setting.\n\nSource. #13064, eff 7-1-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-c6900.html"
